---
description: Keep every current UI language complete whenever copy or a language is added
alwaysApply: true
---

# Current languages

Source of truth: `Lang` and `languages` in `app/permit-engine.ts`. The site must fully support every code listed there. Do not add a language to the switcher until every copy table is complete.

## When adding or changing copy

Every user-facing string must exist for **all current `Lang` keys** in the same change. That includes `ui`, `questions`, `options`, `routeText`, `actionText`, `docText`, `layers` in `app/permit-engine.ts`; `extras` in `app/page.tsx`; and `historyUi` plus every `title`/`body` in `app/history.ts`.

- Type new copy maps as `Record<Lang, …>` so a missing language fails the typecheck.
- Translate for the user; do not leave another language as English, empty, or a machine-placeholder.
- Date formatting uses `dateLocales` in `app/history.ts` — add a locale when `Lang` grows.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — English-only, or a new key missing in other languages
ui.en.start = "Find my route";
historyUi.en.lead = "…"; // other Lang keys unchanged

// ✅ GOOD — same key, every current language
ui.en.start = "Find my route";
ui.de.start = "Meinen Weg finden";
ui.fr.start = "Trouver ma voie";
ui.it.start = "Trova il mio percorso";
ui.rm.start = "Chattar mia via";
```

## When adding a language

Update `Lang`, `languages`, every `Record<Lang, …>` table above, `dateLocales`, and the Languages list in `README.md`. Then add a **product** History entry (users can now use the site in that language).

Do not require translating `index.html` meta tags (document language stays `en`) or code comments.
